#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/change_help.html:7
#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/change_help.html:17
#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/list_help.html:7
#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/list_help.html:17
msgid "How to read this page"
msgstr "Comment lire cette page"

#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/change_help.html:18
msgid ""
"One question and how it was answered, section by section. Nothing here can "
"be edited."
msgstr ""
"Une question et la manière dont elle a été traitée, section par section. "
"Rien ne peut être modifié ici."

#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/change_help.html:25
msgid "The decision, the level and the full text the asker received."
msgstr ""
"La décision, le niveau et le texte complet reçu par la personne qui a posé "
"la question."

#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/change_help.html:27
msgid "Kept sentences"
msgstr "Phrases conservées"

#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/change_help.html:28
msgid ""
"Each sentence of the answer, with the quote from the Bayyinat book that "
"supports it. The quote was checked in code against the source text."
msgstr ""
"Chaque phrase de la réponse, avec la citation du livre Bayyinat qui l’étaye. "
"La citation a été vérifiée par le code dans le texte source."

#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/change_help.html:30
msgid "Removed sentences"
msgstr "Phrases retirées"

#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/change_help.html:31
msgid ""
"Sentences the AI wrote but the checks removed before the answer was shown: "
"the quote was not found in the sources, or it did not support the sentence."
msgstr ""
"Phrases écrites par l’IA mais retirées par les vérifications avant "
"l’affichage de la réponse : la citation était introuvable dans les sources, "
"ou elle n’étayait pas la phrase."

#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/change_help.html:34
msgid ""
"The search query the AI wrote and the passages found, best match first. "
"Click the title to open it."
msgstr ""
"La requête de recherche écrite par l’IA et les passages trouvés, du plus "
"pertinent au moins pertinent. Cliquez sur le titre pour l’ouvrir."

#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/change_help.html:37
msgid ""
"The model used, the response time, the tokens and any error. Click the title "
"to open it."
msgstr ""
"Le modèle utilisé, le temps de réponse, les jetons et une éventuelle erreur. "
"Cliquez sur le titre pour l’ouvrir."

#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/change_help.html:41
#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/list_help.html:90
msgid "Close"
msgstr "Fermer"

#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/list_help.html:18
msgid ""
"Every question asked on the site, with what the AI did with it. Open a "
"question to see its answer sentence by sentence, each with the quote from "
"the book that supports it, and the sentences the checks removed."
msgstr ""
"Chaque question posée sur le site, avec ce que l’IA en a fait. Ouvrez une "
"question pour voir sa réponse phrase par phrase, chacune avec la citation du "
"livre qui l’étaye, ainsi que les phrases retirées par les vérifications."

#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/list_help.html:27
msgid "Asker"
msgstr "Auteur de la question"

#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/list_help.html:28
msgid ""
"The account's email when the person was logged in; Anonymous otherwise. "
"Asking needs no account."
msgstr "L’e-mail du compte si la personne était connectée, sinon « Anonyme ». Poser une question ne nécessite pas de compte."

#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/list_help.html:32
msgid "Decision"
msgstr "Décision"

#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/list_help.html:33
msgid "What the AI did with the question."
msgstr "Ce que l’IA a fait de la question."

#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/list_help.html:36
msgid "Answered from the sources."
msgstr "Répondue à partir des sources."

#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/list_help.html:38
msgid "The sources cover only part of the question; the asker is told so."
msgstr ""
"Les sources ne couvrent qu’une partie de la question ; la personne en est "
"informée."

#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/list_help.html:40
msgid ""
"Sent to the center's specialists: a personal ruling, or a question the "
"sources do not cover."
msgstr ""
"Envoyée aux spécialistes du centre : un avis religieux personnel, ou une "
"question que les sources ne couvrent pas."

#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/list_help.html:42
msgid "No reliable answer could be given; the asker gets a fixed reply."
msgstr ""
"Aucune réponse fiable n’a pu être donnée ; la personne reçoit une réponse "
"fixe."

#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/list_help.html:44
msgid "Not about Islam; the asker gets a fixed reply."
msgstr "Ne concerne pas l’islam ; la personne reçoit une réponse fixe."

#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/list_help.html:49
msgid "Level"
msgstr "Niveau"

#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/list_help.html:50
msgid "Set by the AI before it answers."
msgstr "Fixé par l’IA avant de répondre."

#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/list_help.html:53
msgid "A settled fact about Islam: beliefs, pillars, history."
msgstr "Un fait établi sur l’islam : croyances, piliers, histoire."

#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/list_help.html:55
msgid "An explanation or an argument: wisdom, objections, comparisons."
msgstr "Une explication ou un argument : sagesse, objections, comparaisons."

#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/list_help.html:57
msgid "A matter on which recognized scholars differ; the answer says so."
msgstr ""
"Une question sur laquelle les savants reconnus divergent ; la réponse le "
"précise."

#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/list_help.html:59
msgid ""
"A personal religious ruling (fatwa) about the asker's own situation. Always "
"referred to specialists, never answered by the AI."
msgstr ""
"Un avis religieux personnel (fatwa) sur la situation de la personne. "
"Toujours transmis aux spécialistes, jamais traité par l’IA."

#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/list_help.html:67
msgid "Response time"
msgstr "Temps de réponse"

#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/list_help.html:68
msgid ""
"Seconds from the question to the answer: search, writing and verification of "
"every sentence."
msgstr ""
"Secondes entre la question et la réponse : recherche, rédaction et "
"vérification de chaque phrase."

#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/list_help.html:71
msgid "Tokens"
msgstr "Jetons"

#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/list_help.html:72
msgid ""
"Text sent to the AI model (in) and received from it (out). The cost of an "
"answer depends on these numbers."
msgstr ""
"Texte envoyé au modèle d’IA (entrée) et reçu de lui (sortie). Le coût d’une "
"réponse dépend de ces nombres."

#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/list_help.html:75
msgid "Error"
msgstr "Erreur"

#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/list_help.html:77
msgid "The run completed normally."
msgstr "L’exécution s’est terminée normalement."

#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/list_help.html:79
msgid ""
"A step failed and the asker got a fixed reply; the details are on the "
"question's page."
msgstr ""
"Une étape a échoué et la personne a reçu une réponse fixe ; les détails sont "
"sur la page de la question."

#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/list_help.html:85
msgid "Search"
msgstr "Recherche"

#: qa/templates/admin/qa/question/list_help.html:86
msgid ""
"By question text or asker email, or paste the follow-up number given to the "
"asker."
msgstr "Par le texte de la question ou l’e-mail de son auteur, ou collez le numéro de suivi donné à la personne."
